Author: Nik <nikolaiorl@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 28 03:39:55 2026 +0000

    tui: stop previewFit's no-live-pane return latching a fitted session (task 035)
    
    The no-live-pane closure return in previewFit reported the same previewFitDone{sessionID} message as a real fit, so the handler latched previewFitSessionID either way -- refusing every future fit for that session ID for the rest of the model's lifetime even after its pane later became live again while the row stayed (or was re-)selected. previewFitDone now carries noLivePane (zero value false, preserving every pre-existing test literal), set only on that one return path, and the handler skips latching when it is set. Counts checked against task 034's pre-derived prediction (docs/reports/phase3g-034-previewfit-derivation): all 7 exact-count assertions in preview.feature and interactive_sigwinch_budget.feature are unchanged, zero deltas, no scenario touched. Evidence in docs/reports/phase3g-035-previewfit-no-live-pane-latch/, including a throwaway (never committed) forced-red run proving preview.feature's has-never-been-taller-than assertion still fails before the SIGWINCH count assertion it protects.

